# Fermat's Last Theorem
subtitle: "Why two squares can make a square but two cubes never make a cube — and how a strange curve finally proved it, 358 years after Fermat's margin note."
thumb: "notebook band \"Too big for the margin\" note \"358 years\""

## Fermat's Last Theorem
domain:
    x:
      - -1.8
      - 2.6
    'y':
      - -4
      - 4
    box:
      x: 30
      'y': 150
      w: 480
      h: 480
sources:
    - id: wiles
      title: Modular elliptic curves and Fermat's Last Theorem
      authors: Wiles
      year: 1995
      finding: Semistable elliptic curves are modular; FLT follows
    - id: tw
      title: Ring-theoretic properties of certain Hecke algebras
      authors: Taylor and Wiles
      year: 1995
      finding: Closed the gap in Wiles's 1993 proof
    - id: ribet
      title: On modular representations of Gal(Q̄/Q) arising from modular forms
      authors: Ribet
      year: 1990
      finding: Frey's curve cannot be modular

